Adaptive learning platforms (Khan Academy, Carnegie Learning) that personalise instruction pace show 30–50% greater learning gains per hour than standardised classroom instruction.
The Stanford Online High School serves gifted students from 60 countries; its graduates enter Ivy League universities at rates comparable to top traditional high schools — demonstrating rigour is achievable online.
Meta-analyses consistently show that hybrid (blended) learning outperforms both fully online and fully in-person instruction — the best evidence is for combining the strengths of both.
